  "description": "As one of our most versatile bikes, the Bonero offers you countless possibilities to let it all out – its low weight and steep seat angle offer great climbing characteristics so that you don't exhaust yourself on the way to the trail. The progressive geometry with a flat head angle and long reach gives the bike stability at high speeds and will inspire you to push your limits. The adapted rear triangle lengths in all frame sizes ensure a balanced relationship between front and rear triangle and thus a nimble and agile riding experience. In addition to the classic size recommendations, the six frame sizes also give you the option of selecting the right size for your intended use - if you care about a particularly agile and playful riding feel, this can be achieved with a smaller frame size, while a larger size offers more stable riding behaviour at high speeds. ¹ approx. 13.4 kg, may vary by up to +/- 5 % due to manufacturing tolerances, weight for Warm Grey frame, size L, without pedals.",
